From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:46:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 106/110] vif1: unpack the three dominant unsigned modes
 without per-vector branching

A full match executes 22.4M UNPACKs; 0x6c/0x6d/0x6e with cl=wl=4, MASK off and
unsigned are 94% of the calls. With cl>=wl the destination is sequential, so the
general loop reduces to a straight walk; the fast path copies 16 bytes, widens
four uint16 or four uint8 per vector and falls back for every other case.
PS2X_VIF_UNPACK_FAST=0 restores the general loop and PS2X_VIF_UNPACK_VERIFY=1
runs both and compares the destination words and ROW.

